      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Gentle parenting prioritizes emotional connection over clear boundaries, which can inadvertently allow children to avoid the consequences of their actions and undermining their situational skills. By consistently avoiding harsh discipline, parents may fail to model appropriate conflict resolution, potentially leading to impulsive decision-making in children that they lack the metacognitive tools to regulate. Additionally, a strategy reliant on \"framed\" justifications for child misbehavior can foster a lack of accountability and a fragile sense of self-discipline.\nUltimately, without the challenge of consistent, fair correction, children are less likely to develop the critical life skills of self-regulation and resilience that are essential for navigating the wider world independently.",
